<protocol name="market_intelligence" type="decision" domain="product">

## PURPOSE

Guide market research for naming conventions, competitive positioning, and segment identification. Transform generic product descriptions into market-ready intelligence.

---

## CORE PRINCIPLE: MARKET LANGUAGE

> **Products sell when named how customers SEARCH.**

Your research must answer: "What words do buyers use to find this?"

---

## NAMING CONVENTION RESEARCH

### Three Levels of Naming

| Level | Purpose | Pattern |
|-------|---------|---------|
| Family | Groups related products | Material + Category ("[Material] [Category]") |
| Product | Individual item identity | [DIFFERENTIATOR] + Type + [SIZE] |
| SKU | Unique variant | Family-Attribute-Attribute-Sequence |

### Research Queries for Naming

**Query Pattern:** `[product type] [material] naming ecommerce [market]`

**What to extract:**
- Word order (Material-Size-Function vs Function-Material-Size)
- Common qualifiers (Premium, Heavy-Duty, Professional)
- Size conventions (ml, L, Small/Medium/Large)
- Style terminology (Modern, Classic, Industrial, Artisan)

### Variant Axis Naming

For multi-variant products, identify:
- Which axis is PRIMARY differentiator (Size vs Design vs Color)
- How market structures variant names
- Set vs individual naming patterns

**Query Pattern:** `[category] size variants naming convention`

---

## COMPETITIVE POSITIONING

### Segment Identification

| Segment | Signals | Research Focus |
|---------|---------|----------------|
| Utility/Value | Basic materials, minimal features | Commodity pricing, bulk terms |
| Standard | Expected quality, common materials | Market average, feature parity |
| Premium | Enhanced features, quality materials | Differentiation language, premium markers |
| Luxury | Exceptional materials, exclusivity | Aspirational language, brand terms |

### Position Research Queries

**Query Pattern:** `[product type] wholesale [market] price range`
**Query Pattern:** `[product type] premium vs standard features`

**What to extract:**
- Price bands by segment
- Feature expectations per segment
- Quality markers (certifications, materials)
- Differentiation factors

### Differentiation Discovery

Research what makes products stand out:
- Texture patterns (honeycomb, ribbed, smooth)
- Material grades (food-grade, cosmetic-grade)
- Finish types (matte, glossy, metallic)
- Design elements (printed, embossed, transparent)

---

## MARKET TERMINOLOGY

### Category-Specific Vocabulary

| Category | Key Terms to Research |
|----------|----------------------|
| Containers | Storage, organization, airtight, stackable |
| Kitchenware | Food-safe, dishwasher-safe, microwave-safe |
| Hardware | Heavy-duty, rust-proof, load capacity |
| Decor | Artisan, handcrafted, vintage, contemporary |
| Cosmetics | Premium, luxury, professional, salon-grade |

### Search Term Research

**Query Pattern:** `how customers search [product type] online india`

**What to extract:**
- Common search phrases
- Long-tail keywords
- Problem-based searches ("[feature] [product] for [use case]")
- Use-case searches ("[activity] [products]")

---

## TAG GENERATION

### Tag Categories

| Type | Examples | Purpose |
|------|----------|---------|
| Category | kitchen-storage, home-decor | Browse navigation |
| Material | pet-plastic, brass, ceramic | Filter search |
| Feature | airtight, stackable, microwave-safe | Feature search |
| Use-case | meal-prep, gifting, pantry | Intent matching |
| Style | premium, vintage, modern | Aesthetic matching |

### Tag Quality Rules

- Use hyphenated compound terms (food-safe not "food safe")
- 8-15 tags per product (comprehensive but focused)
- Include both broad and specific terms
- Match actual search behavior

---

## DESCRIPTION GENERATION

### SEO Description Formula

```
[Feature headline]. [Material/quality statement]. [Use case/benefit]. [Call-to-action or differentiator].
```

**Example:**
"Premium [material] [product] with [decorative feature] and [texture]. [Grade] [product] perfect for [primary use]. [Closure type] keeps contents fresh. Ideal for [secondary uses]."

### Description Checklist

- [ ] Primary feature/benefit in first sentence
- [ ] Material and quality callouts
- [ ] Use cases mentioned
- [ ] Keywords naturally integrated
- [ ] 2-3 sentences (50-100 words)

---

## UNIT OF MEASURE (UoM)

### UoM Research

**Query Pattern:** `how [product type] sold wholesale india`

| UoM Type | Question | Common Values |
|----------|----------|---------------|
| Sales | How sold to customer? | Each, Set, Pack, Pair, Dozen |
| Inventory | How stocked? | Pieces, Units, Sets |
| Purchase | How bought from supplier? | Cartons, Cases, Pallets, Boxes |

### Category Defaults

| Category | Typical Sales UoM | Typical Purchase UoM |
|----------|-------------------|---------------------|
| Containers | Each or Set of N | Carton of 12/24 |
| Hardware | Each or Pack | Box of 50/100 |
| Decor | Each | Carton |
| Bulk items | Kg, Liter | Bag, Drum |

---

## DECISION FLOW

## DECISION FLOW (Parallel Sweep)

```
[Product Identified]
       |
       v
[EXECUTE MARKET SWEEP VOLLEY]
   |--> Query: "[product] naming convention ecommerce [market]"
   |--> Query: "[product] price range wholesale [market]"
   |--> Query: "how customers search for [product] [market]"
   |--> Query: "[product] size variations market standard"
   |
   v
[Synthesize Strategy]
   |
   +-> Naming Profile
   +-> Pricing Bands
   +-> SEO Keywords
   +-> UoM Plan
```

**One Volley, All Answers.** Do not iterate unless the sweep completely fails.

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

### Wrong: Generic Names

```
WRONG: "[Generic Category]"
RIGHT: "[Design] [Material] [Category] [Size]"
```

### Wrong: Assumed Positioning

```
WRONG: "This is a premium product" (no evidence)
RIGHT: "Premium positioning supported by: [feature] ([X%] premium in market),
       [design element], [quality indicator]. Similar [feature] items at [price range A] vs
       plain at [price range B]."
```

### Wrong: Missing Context

```
WRONG:
Tags: ["[category]", "storage", "[material]"]

RIGHT:
Tags: ["[material]-storage-[product]", "kitchen-organization", "[category]-[product]",
       "[certification]", "airtight", "pantry-storage", "[use-case]",
       "[design]-print", "premium-[product]", "gift-set"]
```

